<h2 id="sources">Sources &amp; limitations</h2>
<p>This portfolio uses a deliberately small public knowledge base. Current academic status and the Princeton visiting appointment were supplied by Evie. Her <a href="https://github.com/houx15/houx15.github.io/blob/40acdb33c13f878907e88f86319442715c398b3d/about/index.html">earlier public profile</a> records the Tsinghua degrees and September 2024 entry to Peking University’s Center for Social Research. The introduction’s statement of approach is editable self-description, not a measured achievement.</p>
<p>The <a href="/projects/">project case studies</a> distinguish repository design, specific public commits attributed to <code>houx15</code>, and outcomes that have not been independently verified. Citations use fixed revisions where possible. AI coauthors are identified where recorded; repository ownership is not treated as proof of sole authorship. This review did not run the three project applications or reproduce their research results.</p>
<ul>
<li><code>mind-imprint</code> is the verified repository name. A later public branding commit names its English interface “The Mark of Thinking.”</li>
<li>“Knowia” is a user-supplied project name. Its repository has not yet been verified, so no project description or result is asserted.</li>
<li>The visible radar uses labeled, editable example values pending Evie’s self-assessment. It is not an objective capability rating. The academic path shows verified milestones and the concurrent visiting appointment; unspecified dates remain unspecified. Its spacing is not an elapsed-time scale, and it has no wellbeing values or inferred emotional history.</li>
</ul>
<h2>About the AI portfolio assistant</h2>
<p>The current assistant is an interactive local demo with authored, topic-matched answers. It does not call an LLM. Questions stay in this page’s memory and disappear on reload. It cannot access the computer, private files, secrets, personal chat history, or location. Device time is used locally to select a greeting.</p>
<p>Only curated facts and explicitly listed source links are available to the guide. For anything outside those facts, it says it does not know. The site also supports an optional live mode, which is disabled until a server and provider are configured. If offered, it requires explicit opt-in before sending each question (without conversation history) to the site’s server and DeepSeek. A broad time-of-day category is sent for the greeting; no location is requested. A live model selects relevant facts and greeting wording from the reviewed public collection. The server validates the selected IDs and supplies the original wording and citation links; the model cannot invent new URLs or factual wording. Selection can still be mistaken. Provider retention policies apply, and visitors should not submit private information. The service does not log questions; its usage controls retain only aggregate request counts and short-lived hashed connection identifiers.</p>
